course: dictionary
lesson: 5509
title: Many meanings of lazy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word lazy has more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one. «She sat on the sofa all day and would not lift a finger» shows lazy means not wanting to work or try hard.
explain: Look at «a lazy beginning that suddenly turns into a wild, dreamy adventure». Here lazy describes a slow, relaxed start, with no hurry at all. The adventure that follows is the exciting part.
explain: Lazy can also describe work done with little effort, as in «lazy writing». Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Lazy is an adjective: lazy, lazier, laziest.
fact: «Lazy» means not wanting to work, try hard or move about.
fact: «Lazy» can mean slow and relaxed, without hurry, as in «a lazy river».
fact: «Lazy» can describe careless work done with little effort.
fact: «Idle» and «sluggish» are similar in meaning, and «hard-working» is the opposite of lazy.
exercise: In «The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog», what does lazy mean? | Wet from the rain | *Not moving much or in a hurry | Very fast and clever | Hungry for food
exercise: Which word means about the same as lazy in «a lazy Sunday»? | Busy | Angry | *Relaxed | Noisy
exercise: Your teacher writes, «Your writing is lazy, so try again.» What does lazy mean here? | Very long and full of stories | *Done with little effort | Written in gold ink | Funny to read
test: «A lazy river winds slowly through the green fields.» What does lazy mean in this sentence? | Cold to touch | *Slow and calm, without hurry | Fast and rushing | Dirty and muddy
test: Which word is the opposite of lazy? | Sluggish | Idle | *Hard-working | Relaxed
exam: Mum says, «You are being lazy with your maths homework.» What does lazy suggest? | Doing it quickly and neatly | Enjoying a holiday | Asking for help too often | *Not trying hard or putting in effort
